  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional strengthening for Caritas Diocesana Baucau</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of CAFOD&#x2019;s exit strategy for Timor Leste, this project will support a long-standing Church partner, Caritas Diocesana Baucau (CDB), to strengthen their human resources for implementing activities that aim to increase income for rural households in Lautem district in eastern Timor Leste. 
 
Key areas for support identified by CDB together with CAFOD programme staff in this final period of partnership are:
&#x2022; Report and proposal writing,
&#x2022; Monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E), 
&#x2022; Participatory Rural Appraisal (PRA), in order to help CDB to more strongly incorporate the knowledge and opinions of beneficiaries in the planning and management of their projects.
 
Training and support will be delivered by a Progressio Development Worker (on report and proposal writing) and by CAFOD partner KSI (on M&amp;E and PRA).
 
In addition, CDB have also identified that their target groups need further support in book keeping and monitoring of their own levels of production and income generation. CAFOD partner CDC also work with livelihoods groups in the same village, therefore CDC and CDB will conduct joint training for their groups on book keeping and M&amp;E. 
 
CAFOD&#x2019;s Programme Accompanier based in Timor Leste will provide close support for each of these processes.
 
As well as building CDB&#x2019;s institutional capacity and strengthening internal governance and transparency within the target groups, this project will also serve to increase cooperation between local NGOs working on sustainable livelihoods in Timor Leste.</narrative>
  </description>
